      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10095688::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The starting alloy has demonstrated high strength and fatigue resistance.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Exposure near 750 °C for 10, 25, and 50 hours under oxidizing and reducing gases provides a controlled comparison of temporal degradation.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10095688::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "At elevated temperature, Al and Ti preferentially oxidize and diffuse toward the alloy surface.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Oxidizing atmospheres cause rapid formation of a continuous, coherent scale rich in Al and Ti oxides.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Al- and Ti-rich oxide scale limits further oxygen ingress and bulk degradation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The protective scale preserves the fcc matrix under oxidizing conditions.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The protective scale causes better retention of mechanical performance under oxidizing conditions.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reducing H2-containing atmospheres inhibit formation or persistence of the protective oxide scale.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The absence or transient nature of the scale in reducing atmospheres permits more extensive internal oxidation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reducing exposure can destabilize phases in the alloy.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reducing exposure produces greater degradation depth and more rapid mechanical-property loss than oxidizing exposure.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The untreated alloy has minimal degradation after brief high-temperature exposure.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed mechanism is applicable around 750 °C over atmospheres ranging from strongly oxidizing to strongly reducing.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Oxide identity, thickness, and formation kinetics may vary with small compositional or processing differences.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
